nts it spent FY23–25 building — with the core laminates engine printing a record ~INR 400 cr EBITDA (FY26 laminate margin ~16%, Q4 exit ~17%), while the two new businesses (Plywood & Allied, chipboard) are still pre-breakeven and dragged PAT down 18% to INR 56 cr on their losses plus higher interest and depreciation. The investable inflection is operating leverage: management guides FY27 to ~18% top-line growth with no new major capacity (only 2 brownfield laminate lines coming end-FY27) and expects both plywood and chipboard to hit EBITDA breakeven in FY27 — i.e. the loss-making drag turns neutral-to-positive just as the heavy-capex phase ends.","trig":[]},"lm":"","m":6450,"mem":0,"pdd":"","prev_stage":null,"prev_zone_vpe":null,"r":null,"s":"GREENLAM","sig":"","sx":{"SMA_50":"253.3","base_count":"","drawdown_from_prev_signal":"","duration_from_prev_signal":"","pct_below_52w_high":"9.0","pct_change_from_prev_signal":"","pivot_close":"","pivot_low":"","stage_changed_since_prev_signal":"","vpe_df_60d_sum":"-0.6","vpe_zone_cumul_df":""},"t":""}},"s":"GREENLAM"}